      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ridgeville_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the 1840s, an influx of settlers arrived in the region, transforming the landscape from wilderness to farming communities focused on crops such as corn, cotton, and livestock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ridgeville_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Ridgeville is the only community in Etowah County with a black majority, making it unique in the county’s demographic landscape.",
